<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Sample whitelist. Domains you trust yourself with.

    On a whitelisted page the app stops being a dead end: an address bar appears
    and links work, across the domain and all its subdomains. Follow a link off
    the list and the normal behaviour returns — that page renders once, and then
    nothing on it goes anywhere.

    Typing an off-list URL into the address bar does not get that one page. It
    closes the app instead, or the bar would be a way to read anything on the
    web one page at a time.

    The blocklist still wins. A domain in both files is blocked.

    One <item> per domain, same rules as blocklist.xml: no scheme, no "www.",
    subdomains included, sibling domains are separate names.

    The real build usually does not use this file. Set NOPE_WHITELIST to a
    comma-separated list and it replaces everything here:

        NOPE_WHITELIST="example.com,example.org" ./build.sh

    Leave the array empty to get the original no-address-bar app back.
-->
<resources>
    <string-array name="whitelisted_domains">
        <item>chrisincode.com</item>
    </string-array>
</resources>
